{# Explains directory structure and important paths for agents #}

## Environment

### Directory Structure
```
/testcase/                      # Artifact output directory (REQUIRED)
├── base_commit_hash            # Current commit hash
├── repo_changes.diff           # Source code changes (if any)
├── packages.txt                # Installed packages (if any)
├── model_patch.diff            # Final patch file (Fixer)
└── [PoC files]                 # Exploit artifacts (Exploiter)

{{ work_dir }}/                 # Repository directory
└── [source code]               # Vulnerable codebase

/src/
├── build.sh                    # Build script (EDIT THIS)
└── [other sources]

/usr/local/bin/
└── secb                        # SEC-bench helper script
```

### Key Paths
| Path | Purpose | Phase |
|------|---------|-------|
| `{{ work_dir }}` | Repository location | All |
| `/testcase` | Artifact output directory | All |
| `/src/build.sh` | Build script to improve | Build |
| `/usr/local/bin/secb` | Helper script (edit `repro()` function) | Exploit |
| `/testcase/base_commit_hash` | Commit hash file | Build |
| `/testcase/model_patch.diff` | Final patch | Fix |

### Helper Commands
- `secb build` - Build project with sanitizers
- `secb repro` - Run PoC (calls `repro()` function in `/usr/local/bin/secb`)
- `secb patch` - Apply `/testcase/model_patch.diff`

**NOTE:** The repository is already cloned at `{{ work_dir }}`. DO NOT clone again.
